infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title useTransition vs useDeferredValue
  desc Same interruptible background render — the split is who owns the value
  compares
    - label useTransition
      children
        - label You own the setState
          desc Wrap setQuery in startTransition inside your own handler
        - label isPending for free
          desc Built-in honest signal to dim the stale-but-visible content
        - label Split the state
          desc Urgent value echoes the input, transition value drives the heavy tree
        - label Keep the manipulated value urgent
          desc Never put the directly-typed echo inside the transition
    - label useDeferredValue
      children
        - label You receive the value
          desc Prop from a parent, router, or library hook — no setter to wrap
        - label Compare for staleness
          desc deferred !== current marks the stale render to dim
        - label Memoize the subtree
          desc On the deferred value, or you pay the full cost twice per keystroke
        - label Cheap urgent render first
          desc Holds the old value, then catches up in a background transition
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
